This product depends on github.com/superfly/ltx (Copyright Fly.io, Inc.,
licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0), which defines the LTX
transaction-segment format offshoot uses for durable storage. See go.mod for
the full set of third-party dependencies and their respective licenses.

offshoot's WAL capture engine (internal/capture) uses a technique publicly
described by Litestream (github.com/benbjohnson/litestream, Apache License,
Version 2.0) — holding a long-running read transaction on a dedicated SQLite
connection to prevent foreign checkpoints from restarting the WAL out from
under an in-progress capture. offshoot's implementation was independently
written against the public SQLite WAL file format and Litestream's
published description of that approach; no Litestream source code was
copied, vendored, or adapted into this repository. See
docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-29-offshoot-capture-spike.md and
docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-29-offshoot-spike-report.md for the
implementation record.
